  "assessment_outcome": "insufficient_information",
  "explanation": "The patient reports possible hearing loss in the left ear but has no audiometry or audiogram available. The clinical standard for commercial drivers requires unaided hearing loss ≥40 dB in the better ear to be unfit for an unconditional licence. Without objective audiometric data, it is impossible to determine if this threshold is met. Furthermore, a conditional licence depends on whether the standard can be met with a hearing aid; however, no hearing aid has been fitted or tested, and there is no evidence regarding the patient's ability to meet standards with amplification. The nurse note confirms the absence of audiometry but does not provide verified facts establishing either fitness or unfitness. Therefore, no established restriction or conditional permission can be derived from the supplied evidence.",
